| Scenario | Recommended Method | Why? |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Simple website / Small app** | **Method 1 (History API)** | Quickest to implement with minimal code. |
| **Complex App / SEO needs** | **Method 2 (Query Params)** | Allows users to bookmark or share the "modal open" state. |
| **Large Scale SPA** | **Method 3 (Nested Routes)** | Best for maintainability and follows standard web patterns. |

### ⚠️ A Note on UX
When you implement this, ensure that your **"Close" button** also triggers a `history.back()` (or a router back). If the user clicks the "X" button and stays on the page, but you haven't removed that "history entry," the next time they hit the back button, they will still be looking at the (now hidden) modal state.

